   "title": "Figure 25. Low-side switch",
   "page": 12,
   "description": "A solenoid hangs from the battery and is switched to ground by a PWM-driven MOSFET; the shunt sits between the solenoid and the switch, so it stays in the current loop when the switch opens and the recirculating current through the clamp diode is measured too. With the switch on the inputs sit near ground; with it off the clamp holds them a diode drop above the battery. A short to ground can also be seen.",
